# The 1954 MIT Summer Session notes, "Digital Computers: Advanced Coding
# Techniques", lecture 13, p. 13-3: the same two differential equations as
# E-364 p. 18, "Our program might be".
#
# As printed, the last two equations have no commas (k = t - 10.1 and CP 1),
# which the rules require; they are put in here. As printed it also has no
# PRINT, so it integrates from t = 2 to t = 10.5 and types nothing at all.
# The PRINT at the end is added so that there is something to see.
    t = 2,
    h = 0.5,
    y|1 = 0,
    y|2 = 0,
1   D y|1 = y|2 + 1,
    D y|2 = -y|1,
    k = t - 10.1,
    CP 1,
    PRINT t, y|1, y|2.
    STOP
